      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "EL MYSTRO (5) is a progressive gelding who was an impressive 17m winner two back at Pinjarra before he did some work but stuck on for a 2.5m second in the Westbred 3CG Classic at Gloucester Park last time. Similar draw here and should be peaking fourth up. Big chance. IDEAL BEACH (8) is the horse that beat EL MYSTRO in the Westbred Classic and it was a tough performance as he raced three without cover but toughed it out, making it two wins on the trot. If things go his way from the back line he can deliver again. HAVTIMEFORMIKI NZ (6) has placed in his two city outings since kicking off his campaign with back-to-back wins. Reliable colt who looms as a serious challenger. PATRIARCH NZ (2) has improved with each outing this time in, culminating in a last start win at Pinjarra. This is stronger but he is at his peak now and is aided by a good draw.",
